    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Miss Anthony returns for her three-month review. She has had no swelling for six weeks and climbs stairs without stopping. Her morning weight has held at 56.0 to 56.4 kg for a month. She has resumed a reduced lecture schedule and walks a mile a day. She has had no dizziness on spironolactone, no breast tenderness, and no muscle cramps. She asks whether she still needs the daily water pill, because it limits her travel. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>No edema for six weeks; stairs without stopping</td></tr><tr><td>Weight diary</td><td>Stable at 56.0 to 56.4 kg for a month</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>No dizziness, breast tenderness, or cramps on spironolactone</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Walking a mile a day; reduced lecture schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Patient goal</td><td>Fewer diuretic days so she can travel</td></tr><tr><td>NYHA class</td><td>I to II</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

