    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, euvolemic (I50.32)</content>. Dry weight 56 kg reached, with no congestion on examination. NT-proBNP has fallen from 1650 to 720 pg/mL and the KCCQ-12 has risen from 52 to 70. Potassium 4.5 on spironolactone. [S]<list><item>Change furosemide to as needed, for a weight gain of more than 1 kg in a day or 2 kg in a week.</item><item>Continue empagliflozin and spironolactone.</item><item>Written travel plan: weigh each morning on the road and carry furosemide.</item><item>Basic metabolic panel at the six-month review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertensive heart disease (I11.0)</content>. Blood pressure 132/74 mmHg, nearly at the 130/80 target. [S]<list><item>No change; recheck at the six-month review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel with magnesium</td><td>1 to 2 weeks after starting or changing therapy; every 3 to 6 months when stable</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Potassium 4.5, eGFR 61. This is the first panel since spironolactone started three months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel 1 to 2 weeks after starting spironolactone</td><td>Once, after starting a mineralocorticoid antagonist</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not drawn in the two-week window, a deviation from the protocol. Today&apos;s potassium and kidney function are normal, so no harm resulted; the reminder is now in her chart</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>NT-proBNP</td><td>Selectively in outpatient follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>720 pg/mL, down from 1650; informs decongestion, not used to titrate therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure, heart rate, weight, jugular venous pressure, edema, lungs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Euvolemic at 56.2 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>NYHA functional class</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Class I to II</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>KCCQ-12</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>70, up 18 points from baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>Periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Only with unexplained clinical change</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Improving as expected; routine repeat imaging is not recommended</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cardiac rehabilitation</td><td>If exercise tolerance plateaus</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Exercise tolerance still improving with daily walking</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily weight diary and travel plan</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Travel weight plan written today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Reach euvolemia with no ankle edema and a stable dry weight within three months. Outcome by 1905-06-29: Dry weight 56 kg; furosemide changed to as-needed use [S]</item><item>Improve the KCCQ-12 overall summary score by at least 15 points by the three-month review. Outcome by 1905-06-29: KCCQ-12 rose from 52 to 70 [S]</item><item>Lower blood pressure below 130/80 by the six-month review without orthostatic symptoms. In progress; target 1905-09-28 [S]</item><item>Resume a full speaking and travel schedule by the six-month review. In progress; target 1905-09-28 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure (2022); 2023 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on Management of Heart Failure With Preserved Ejection Fraction (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, heart failure monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month heart failure review with a basic metabolic panel and KCCQ-12. Next scheduled visit 1905-09-28: six-month heart failure review. [S]</paragraph></text>

